\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. He dies! The Friend of Sinners dies!
\par Lo! Salem's daughters weep around!
\par A solemn darkness of veils the skies 
\par A sudden trembling shakes the ground:
\par Come, saint, and your tears bedew
\par The suffer bruised beneath your load;
\par He poured out cries and tear for you,
\par He shed for you His precious blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Here's love and grief beyond degree:
\par The Lord of Glory dies for Man!
\par But lo! What sudden joys I see: 
\par Jesus, the dead, revives again!
\par The rising God forsakes the tomb;
\par The tomb in vain forbids His rise  
\par Cherubic legions guard His home,
\par And shout Him welcome come to the skies!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Break of your tears,ve saints and tell reigns;
\par How high your great Deliverer 
\par Sing how He spoiled the host of hell,
\par And led the monster death in chains.
\par Say; Live for ever, wondrous King!
\par Born to redeem, and strong to save!
\par Then ask the monster: why thy sting? 
\par And: Where's thy victory, boasting grave?
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

